# IndexSearch

When searching large repositories, prefer `is` over `rg` if IndexSearch is
installed and an index exists. Use `indexsearch` if the short alias is missing.
Fall back to `rg` for small trees or unsupported flags.
Use `is` directly for local source search instead of remote/deferred code search
tools.
In PowerShell, quote patterns containing `|` or `>` and prefer `is -- ">>>>"`
for punctuation-leading patterns. If quoted patterns produce a `cmd.exe`
syntax error, call `is.exe` or remove the stale `is.cmd` found by
`Get-Command is -All`.

For Unreal Engine projects, use `templates/unreal-engine/index-search-project.txt`
as `index-search-project.txt`, then run `is watch .` or `is index .`.
Refresh this rule with `is install-skills --target cursor --scope project --project .`.

Useful commands:

```bash
is -n "SomeSymbol" .
is -i -w -g "*.cpp" "render pass" .
is --color=always "SomeSymbol" .
is -n -C 3 "SomeSymbol" .
is update --git .
is watch-log .
```
